<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial policy — Settled"
  description="How Settled makes picks, discloses affiliate relationships, and handles corrections."
>
  <h1>Editorial policy</h1>

  <h2>Affiliate disclosure</h2>
  <p>
    Some links on Settled are affiliate links. If you click and buy, we
    may earn a small commission at no extra cost to you. We are an
    Amazon Associate and earn from qualifying purchases. We may also
    participate in other affiliate programs (Impact, ShareASale, CJ
    Affiliate, and direct merchant programs).
  </p>

  <h2>How picks are made</h2>
  <p>
    Each article lays out its criteria in a "What we tested for"
    section. Candidates are evaluated against those criteria. We drop
    any product that fails two or more. Among the survivors, the pick
    is the one we'd keep using a year in.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not accept payment in exchange for inclusion in any article.
    We do not accept free products in exchange for coverage. When we
    test a product the publisher provided (rare), we say so in the
    article.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    If we get something wrong, we update the article and add a
    correction note at the top with the date. We don't silently revise.
  </p>

  <h2>AI tooling disclosure</h2>
  <p>
    Articles on Settled may be drafted with AI assistance. Every
    article is reviewed against the criteria above before publication.
    We never publish AI-generated content without human review.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions, corrections, or merchant inquiries:
    <a href="mailto:hello@settled.world">hello@settled.world</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
